<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Đồng Khánh</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1864–1889</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Dong Khanh</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Đồng Khánh was emperor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vietnam">Vietnam</a> of the Nguyen dynasty from 1885 to 1889. After the regent <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ton-that-thuyet">Tôn Thất Thuyết</a> fled from Huế with the young emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ham-nghi">Hàm Nghi</a> to lead the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/can-vuong">Cần Vương</a> resistance, the French placed Hàm Nghi's elder brother on the throne. He cooperated with the French <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protectorate">protectorate</a> and urged the rebels to submit, and he died after a short reign.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/dong-khanh.jpg" alt="Đồng Khánh" width="320" height="456" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tonkin11h.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
